00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:41.110
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care if
you haven't seen the movie yet.

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:46.410
In Fantastic Beasts 2, Credence goes on a
quest to discover his true identity and after

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:51.190
chasing down a red herring that he's Leta
Lestrange's brother Corvus, in the final scene

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:55.799
Grindelwald tells the young wizard that his
true identity is Aurelius Dumbledore.

00:00:55.799 --> 00:01:00.080
To support this revelation Grindelwald takes
the baby chick that Credence has been taking

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.800
care of and it transforms into a phoenix.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:07.150
Potter fans will know that phoenixes are associated
with the Dumbledore family and Fawkes was

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:11.470
a phoenix who was a companion and protector
to Albus Dumbledore at Hogwarts.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:16.300
This reveal about Credence has shocked Potter
fans as until now the character Aurelius Dumbledore

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:21.320
has never appeared or been mentioned in any
movies or books, which is strange given Grindelwald

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:26.170
predicts that he and Aurelius will "together
go down in history as [they] remake this world."

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:30.560
During the reveal, Grindelwald also tells
Credence that his "brother seeks to destroy"

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:34.060
him, implying that Dumbledore plans to kill
Credence.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:38.730
This patently isn't true as during the movie,
it was Albus who asked Newt to go to Paris

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:40.480
and try to save Credence.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:41.480
In fact, J.K.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:45.079
Rowling herself said in an in an official
featurette released for the film that "whatever

00:01:45.079 --> 00:01:48.140
you think you know at the end of the movie
might not be the case."

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:52.840
So, let's go through all the evidence as to
why Grindelwald could very well be lying.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:58.340
Much is made in the movie about what a master
of persuasion and deception Grindelwald really

00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:59.340
is.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:02.640
Right at the beginning, President Picquery
remarks that they had to cut out the nefarious

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.100
wizard's tongue and change his guard three
times because he's so persuasive.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:11.420
Little did she know that Grindelwald had actually
recruited Abernathy to his cause and switched

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:15.850
places with him, and Abernathy ends up rewarded
with a forked tongue of his own.

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:20.000
In Paris, Grindelwald recruits the bounty
hunter Grimmson who is supposed to be hunting

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.160
down Credence.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:25.520
He also recruits a huge number of wizards
to his cause in the speech he gives at the

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:29.210
end, and he even tricks the sweet-natured
Queenie over to his side, which I'll talk

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:30.550
more about later.

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:34.730
In fact, it feels like Grindelwald is more
than just persuasive; he's actually the man

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:38.360
behind the curtain, a puppet master pulling
on everyone's strings and bamboozling everyone

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:41.660
with red herrings and tricks, all for his
own nefarious ends.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:46.020
For example, when Credence goes to find the
nanny who'd looked after him, the bounty hunter

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:48.930
Grimmson kills her on Grindelwald's orders.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:53.140
It seems like Grindelwald wanted rid of her
to clear up any loose ends and true answers

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:55.250
she might provide to Credence.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:03:00.040
Grindelwald also had the Lestrange family
history moved from the French Ministry archives

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:01.660
to the Lestrange mausoleum.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:06.520
Which raises questions as to why he did that
and what information he might have manipulated.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:10.870
After that scene, Newt points out to Tina
that all these things including "Queenie,

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:15.660
the family tree, it's all been bait" to get
them to the rally that Grindelwald is holding.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:19.080
And you can see during Grindelwald's speech
to the wizarding community that he's very

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:22.440
skilled in rhetoric and manages to convince
many people.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:26.970
He knows how to make his extreme positions
and views sound almost reasonable and sensible

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:27.970
to them.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:31.920
Director David Yates has said that Grindelwald
is quite different to the other big bad we

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.560
all know from the Harry Potter series, Voldemort.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.140
Yates says, "If you disagreed with Voldemort,
he would kill you in an instant.

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:40.560
But Grindelwald is incredibly beguiling.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:45.180
He would rather win people over to his side
than annihilate them, and he is smart enough

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:50.200
to understand you have to win hearts and minds,
not coerce people, to gain their allegiance."

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:54.709
Which is why I think we can't take what he's
saying to Credence about his identity at face

00:03:54.709 --> 00:03:55.709
value.

00:03:55.709 --> 00:04:00.280
He knows that Credence is desperate to discover
his real identity and so he preys on that

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:02.810
to set Credence against Dumbledore.

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:06.569
He even conjures up a phoenix to bamboozle
him into believing the lie.

00:04:06.569 --> 00:04:10.500
So, why does Grindelwald need to use Credence
against Dumbledore?

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:14.690
Well, in Fantastic Beasts 2 it's shown that
Dumbledore and Grindelwald were lovers when

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:18.120
they were younger and they made a blood pact
where they promised they would never fight

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:19.120
each other.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:23.520
The pendant that Grindelwald wears and which
Newt's niffler steals from him contains drops

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:27.830
of blood from the two wizards and the actual
existence of the pendant seems to physically

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:31.860
prevent Dumbledore and Grindelwald from attacking
each other directly.

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:35.979
At the end of the movie, Newt gives the pendant
to Dumbledore who indicates he will look into

00:04:35.979 --> 00:04:37.740
whether he can destroy it.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:41.800
Part of me wonders if Dumbledore seems a little
reluctant to break the blood pact and whether

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:46.120
he's holding out hope he can turn his old
friend away from the dark path he's chosen.

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:50.840
The other major reason that Grindelwald needs
Credence is because of his immense power as

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:51.870
an Obscurial.

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:56.439
Normally, an Obscurus would have killed its
host by the age of ten but Credence has survived

00:04:56.439 --> 00:05:00.499
into adulthood demonstrating his superior
wizarding powers.

00:05:00.499 --> 00:05:04.719
And in Fantastic Beasts 2, by the end of the
movie we finally see that Credence has gained

00:05:04.719 --> 00:05:06.830
control over his power.

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:11.680
Grindelwald gives him a wand and Credence
uses it to blast away the side of a huge mountain

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.219
in the distance.

00:05:13.219 --> 00:05:17.749
This is in stark contrast to the first movie
where Credence explicitly said he didn't want

00:05:17.749 --> 00:05:20.509
to control his power:
"You can control it.

00:05:20.509 --> 00:05:21.509
Credence."

00:05:21.509 --> 00:05:27.330
"I don't think I want to, Mr. Graves."

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:31.569
Now that Grindelwald has manoeuvred Credence
to his side and he's been able to focus the

00:05:31.569 --> 00:05:36.839
young wizard's rage, he will presumably use
him as a weapon against Dumbledore next.

00:05:36.839 --> 00:05:41.559
Credence is perhaps one of a few wizards powerful
and foolhardy enough to confront Dumbledore

00:05:41.559 --> 00:05:45.430
as remember how earlier in the movie when
Grindelwald asked his followers if they would

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:49.860
go to Hogwarts and attack Dumbledore, not
one of them said they would.

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:54.800
What's interesting about Credence's identity
is that it's changed in every film so far,

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:59.430
meaning it wouldn't surprise me if we discover
Credence's true family line in the next Fantastic

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:00.430
Beasts movie.

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:04.199
He might be connected to an alternate character
from Potter lore.

00:06:04.199 --> 00:06:08.599
After all, we see he's good friends with Nagini
who will end up eventually as Voldemort's

00:06:08.599 --> 00:06:12.249
snake, so could there be a connection between
Credence and Voldemort?

00:06:12.249 --> 00:06:14.360
Let me know what you think.

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:18.610
Another victim of Grindelwald's manipulations
in Fantastic Beasts 2 is Queenie who ends

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:20.979
up becoming a follower of the dark wizard.

00:06:20.979 --> 00:06:25.340
Although I felt her turn to the dark side
was a little abrupt, you can see why she personally

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:29.789
feels attracted to the idea of overturning
the restrictive laws which forbid her from

00:06:29.789 --> 00:06:32.349
having an open relationship with muggle Jacob.

00:06:32.349 --> 00:06:35.800
I do wonder whether any foul play was at work
though.

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:39.469
After all, there was that teapot which kept
trying to serve her more tea.

00:06:39.469 --> 00:06:43.189
So, I wonder whether anything was slipped
into her drink to make her more susceptible

00:06:43.189 --> 00:06:44.389
to Grindelwald's guile.

00:06:44.389 --> 00:06:48.509
There's been quite a bit of discussion in
the fandom that the timeline for Credence

00:06:48.509 --> 00:06:51.649
being Albus Dumbledore's brother is also problematic.

00:06:51.649 --> 00:06:55.529
The main issue people have identified is that
when the first Fantastic Beasts movie came

00:06:55.529 --> 00:07:01.419
out in 2016, Ezra Miller said in an interview
that Credence was 18 years old in that film.

00:07:01.419 --> 00:07:06.179
Fantastic Beasts And Where To Find Them was
set in 1926 which would have made his birthday

00:07:06.179 --> 00:07:08.520
sometime in 1908 or 1907.

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:13.520
And that just doesn't fit very well with the
fact that the books established that Albus

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:18.949
Dumbledore's mother Kendra died in 1899, many
years before Credence's supposed birthdate.

00:07:18.949 --> 00:07:23.029
However, some new evidence just came out via
the original screenplay for The Crimes of

00:07:23.029 --> 00:07:27.809
Grindlewald which indicates that the shipwreck
scene happens in 1901.

00:07:27.809 --> 00:07:32.460
In that scene, Leta Lestrange swapped Credence
with her brother Corvus just before the ship

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:37.939
sunk meaning Credence was a baby in 1901 and
therefore his birth date, say a couple of

00:07:37.939 --> 00:07:43.179
years earlier, would fit roughly with the
year 1899 that Kendra Dumbledore died.

00:07:43.179 --> 00:07:47.569
Now, that still doesn't mean that Credence
is definitely a Dumbledore, it's just that

00:07:47.569 --> 00:07:51.770
some retconning seems to have happened for
Fantastic Beasts 2 to make Credence's age

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:53.449
line up with the Dumbledore reveal.

00:07:53.449 --> 00:07:58.490
So, do you think Grindelwald is lying to Credence
at the end of Fantastic Beasts 2?

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:01.319
And if you do, who do you think Credence really
is?

